1
00:00:21,788 --> 00:00:22,622
All right,

2
00:00:23,656 --> 00:00:24,924
I've made my decision.

3
00:01:14,774 --> 00:01:16,676
Michiko, where are you going?

4
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:17,844
Yeah, come play.

5
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:20,013
I'm in a hurry. Later.

6
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:39,632
Large dumplings please, and make it quick.
I'm starving to death!

7
00:01:41,101 --> 00:01:43,436
Honey, quick! A large order of dumplings!

8
00:01:43,503 --> 00:01:46,372
She said she's starving to death.

9
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:49,409
That lady is always hungry!

10
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,550
I almost got a hamburger,

11
00:01:57,617 --> 00:02:00,153
but this was the right call!

12
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,490
Thank you for waiting.

13
00:02:03,556 --> 00:02:05,959
Thank you!

14
00:02:07,594 --> 00:02:10,630
Ah, my dumplings.

15
00:02:18,938 --> 00:02:19,939
Delicious!

16
00:02:20,573 --> 00:02:21,407
So good!

17
00:02:21,474 --> 00:02:23,076
Give me back my dumplings!

18
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:26,446
I walked all the way here from...
fifth avenue, just to eat this!

19
00:02:26,513 --> 00:02:27,380
Shut it!

20
00:02:28,681 --> 00:02:30,416
You're Japanese, right?

21
00:02:30,483 --> 00:02:33,987
If you're an ideal women,
you must pay respect to your elders!

22
00:02:34,053 --> 00:02:36,789
- Give it back, you dumpling thief!
- Aren't you greedy!

23
00:02:36,856 --> 00:02:38,057
Huh?!

24
00:02:38,525 --> 00:02:41,027
You're the greedy one!

25
00:02:42,495 --> 00:02:44,030
What are they fighting over?

26
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:49,135
What the heck is going on?

27
00:02:49,202 --> 00:02:53,640
Explain to me how something like this
could happen to a hospital...

28
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:56,409
showing the Japanese flag, Director.

29
00:02:56,476 --> 00:02:57,377
Ah...

30
00:02:57,877 --> 00:03:01,281
It is ranked as 38th in the
National hospital ranking this year,

31
00:03:02,048 --> 00:03:06,186
we are taking this very seriously...
very seriously.

32
00:03:06,252 --> 00:03:07,086
Of course,

33
00:03:07,754 --> 00:03:10,790
the Director and I...

34
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:13,793
You must both take responsibility,
and resign.

35
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,128
Please wait.

36
00:03:15,595 --> 00:03:17,030
First we will have...

37
00:03:17,997 --> 00:03:18,998
an investigation,

38
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:21,935
a third party investigation.

39
00:03:22,001 --> 00:03:24,837
I'm sick of hearing those words!

40
00:03:24,904 --> 00:03:26,272
Resign!

41
00:03:26,339 --> 00:03:28,608
We deeply apologise.

42
00:03:29,976 --> 00:03:34,147
The factional disputes and...
authority disagreements

43
00:03:34,914 --> 00:03:37,717
within the hospital have eventually caused

44
00:03:37,784 --> 00:03:41,154
the damage of...the hospital brand.

45
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,889
But…

46
00:03:43,323 --> 00:03:46,025
we will pull together and...

47
00:03:46,092 --> 00:03:47,694
strive to save the hospitals name.

48
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:51,698
Director, how about we stop
resisting the inevitable...

49
00:03:52,165 --> 00:03:55,535
and withdraw gracefully?

50
00:03:55,602 --> 00:03:56,803
Deputy Director...

51
00:03:56,869 --> 00:03:58,838
It's useless.

52
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:01,608
Nothing like this has ever happened.

53
00:04:01,674 --> 00:04:04,744
The only way is for the
two of us to step down,

54
00:04:04,811 --> 00:04:06,779
and trust the hospital in the hands

55
00:04:06,846 --> 00:04:08,815
of the next generation.

56
00:04:15,989 --> 00:04:16,990
Mom!

57
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:18,424
Mom!

58
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:24,430
Mom!

59
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,368
Murphy's sign.

60
00:04:28,701 --> 00:04:29,869
Call an ambulance!

61
00:04:31,738 --> 00:04:32,739
Hurry up!

62
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:34,774
How far along are you?

63
00:04:35,742 --> 00:04:36,809
Thirty weeks.

64
00:04:36,876 --> 00:04:38,211
Does it hurt here?

65
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:39,345
It's no good.

66
00:04:39,412 --> 00:04:40,413
The road is closed...

67
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,949
because there was a shooting.

68
00:04:43,583 --> 00:04:45,018
Acute cholecystitis.

69
00:04:45,385 --> 00:04:47,420
She needs an emergency surgery.

70
00:04:47,487 --> 00:04:50,757
Otherwise, both the mother...
and the baby will be in danger.

71
00:04:50,823 --> 00:04:52,558
Mom! Mom!

72
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:55,228
My hospital is close! Let's go!

73
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,896
- Mom! Mom!
- Let's carry her.

74
00:05:00,433 --> 00:05:02,602
Mom! Mom!

75
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:05,305
- Mom!
- Hurry! This way.

76
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:08,541
- Mom! Mom!
- To the operating room! This way!

77
00:05:08,608 --> 00:05:11,878
- Mom!
- Hurry!

78
00:05:11,944 --> 00:05:13,413
One, two, three.

79
00:05:15,715 --> 00:05:17,450
Mom…

80
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:21,387
Mom! Is my mom going to die?

81
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:22,755
Don't worry,

82
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:24,891
- I won't let her die.
- Really?

83
00:05:26,659 --> 00:05:27,894
I never fail.

84
00:05:40,239 --> 00:05:43,676
Making an incision for an
emergency open course discectomy.

85
00:05:43,743 --> 00:05:45,878
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

86
00:05:58,725 --> 00:06:01,894
The inflamed gallbladder wall
is touching the uterus.

87
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:03,262
Watch out,

88
00:06:03,329 --> 00:06:05,565
the baby's head is right over there.

89
00:06:05,932 --> 00:06:06,999
Got it.

90
00:06:07,066 --> 00:06:09,369
Mobilizing the uterus
off of the gallbladder.

91
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:36,662
Too slow. Drag it here, and open wider.

92
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:38,164
Sorry, got it.

93
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:39,198
Wow.

94
00:06:39,966 --> 00:06:40,800
She's so fast.

95
00:06:41,934 --> 00:06:45,371
She really is going to save the baby.

96
00:06:46,606 --> 00:06:47,940
Who are you?

97
00:06:48,374 --> 00:06:50,243
Just a surgeon passing by.

98
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:51,577
What?

99
00:06:51,644 --> 00:06:53,546
- Three zero nylon.
- Here.

100
00:07:05,691 --> 00:07:06,659
Amazing.

101
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:21,774
All right.

102
00:07:22,675 --> 00:07:25,378
You did great, and your mom too.

103
00:07:32,919 --> 00:07:34,153
Good luck.

104
00:07:36,856 --> 00:07:37,824
Great job.

105
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:43,830
Bravo! Bravo!

106
00:07:57,276 --> 00:07:59,679
Thank you, doctor! Thank you!

107
00:08:03,015 --> 00:08:05,952
I can't do this anymore... I'm so hungry.

108
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:08,287
Dumplings!

109
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:23,035
Ah! The dumpling burglar!

110
00:08:23,102 --> 00:08:25,104
I won't take it this time.

111
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:28,374
It's my treat, so eat up!

112
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:30,409
Thank you for waiting.

113
00:08:32,445 --> 00:08:35,348
That was quite the operation.

114
00:08:35,715 --> 00:08:39,185
American doctors can't perform
such delicate surgeries.

115
00:08:39,552 --> 00:08:42,622
You are the ideal lady after all!

116
00:08:42,989 --> 00:08:44,557
Here, drink up.

117
00:08:44,624 --> 00:08:46,259
So hey, are you...

118
00:08:46,826 --> 00:08:48,461
are you a nurse there?

119
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:50,897
Or could you be a doctor?

120
00:08:54,066 --> 00:08:55,201
Do I look like one?

121
00:08:55,701 --> 00:08:57,003
Not at all!

122
00:08:57,703 --> 00:08:59,305
I'm a cleaning woman.

123
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,641
- I see.
- Here.

124
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:07,446
In American hospitals,

125
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:10,783
treatments and surgeries both
depend on money.

126
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:14,921
Without the money you can
barely get any decent treatment.

127
00:09:14,987 --> 00:09:20,126
I guess they want us poor people to die.
Though they're still better than...

128
00:09:20,192 --> 00:09:24,030
The University Hospitals in Japan
where they choose instructors...

129
00:09:24,096 --> 00:09:26,966
through dumb chair pulling games.

130
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,968
Oh, you know well.

131
00:09:30,269 --> 00:09:31,337
Well,

132
00:09:32,605 --> 00:09:34,707
I was a cleaning lady in Japan too.

133
00:09:36,976 --> 00:09:41,113
It's like the Japanese TV show...

134
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:44,183
where the cleaning lady
witnesses everything.

135
00:09:45,284 --> 00:09:47,620
- No, no... it's the housekeeper.
- Oh, right.

136
00:09:49,388 --> 00:09:52,692
Well, Japanese hospitals
are totally corrupted.

137
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:55,595
They are just a gathering of
old-typed doctors and professors.

138
00:09:55,661 --> 00:09:58,598
What is so good about brown-nosing?

139
00:09:58,664 --> 00:10:00,766
If you have time doing things like that,

140
00:10:01,534 --> 00:10:03,035
care about the patients!

141
00:10:03,936 --> 00:10:05,271
You're right!

142
00:10:05,338 --> 00:10:07,340
We're so alike!

143
00:10:07,406 --> 00:10:08,674
Let's have another.

144
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:10,576
- Huh?
- I'm full.

145
00:10:12,044 --> 00:10:16,716
Good grief, where did Michiko go?
What do you think, Ben Casey?

146
00:10:17,183 --> 00:10:19,752
I wonder if she's eating Sushi
in Kanazawa again.

147
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:23,122
Hello? Michiko? Where are you?

148
00:10:23,489 --> 00:10:24,323
New York.

149
00:10:25,057 --> 00:10:26,592
New York?

150
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:30,630
Last night, a cleaning lady...

151
00:10:30,696 --> 00:10:32,832
treated me to dinner and a massage!

152
00:10:32,898 --> 00:10:37,770
If you're that tight on money,
hurry back home and work.

153
00:10:37,837 --> 00:10:40,406
<i>You are requested by a credible source who</i>

154
00:10:40,473 --> 00:10:43,075
<i>would love to welcome you</i>
<i>to their hospital</i>

155
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:45,945
<i>and are willing to pay</i>
<i>as much as you want!</i>

156
00:10:46,312 --> 00:10:48,514
If you don't come, you're fired.

157
00:10:49,081 --> 00:10:50,816
All right.

158
00:10:55,521 --> 00:10:57,089
Come on! Come on!

159
00:10:57,823 --> 00:10:59,859
- Come on!
- Yeah!

160
00:11:09,635 --> 00:11:11,971
Michiko never fails!

161
00:11:19,211 --> 00:11:22,448
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a female maverick doctor.</i>

162
00:11:26,619 --> 00:11:29,288
TOUTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL
BOARD OF DIRECTORS

163
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:34,126
Today, we leaders,
are taking part in a mass resignation.

164
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:36,996
We hope for the sake of the hospital,

165
00:11:37,063 --> 00:11:40,433
this will create an opportunity for...

166
00:11:40,499 --> 00:11:42,601
the hospital to succeed once again.

167
00:11:44,336 --> 00:11:46,972
We may be resigning,

168
00:11:48,274 --> 00:11:52,078
but the hospital is immortal!

169
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:55,414
Hooray!

170
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:56,782
Hooray!

171
00:11:56,849 --> 00:11:57,883
Hooray!

172
00:11:57,950 --> 00:11:58,984
Hooray!

173
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:00,352
Hooray!

174
00:12:00,419 --> 00:12:01,387
Hooray!

175
00:12:04,123 --> 00:12:05,558
- Hiruma.
- Yes?

176
00:12:06,358 --> 00:12:08,994
Why are you sitting?

177
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:13,265
I'm sorry.
I couldn't find the right timing.

178
00:12:13,332 --> 00:12:14,400
I'm sorry.

179
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:20,439
I, Hiruma Shigekatsu,

180
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:25,111
have a parting gift...

181
00:12:25,845 --> 00:12:28,280
as I take my leave

182
00:12:29,548 --> 00:12:30,983
from the hospital,

183
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:33,586
please accept this.

184
00:12:34,053 --> 00:12:37,957
I called on a super doctor from abroad.

185
00:12:38,023 --> 00:12:38,924
Minami.

186
00:12:46,665 --> 00:12:49,702
- Director Hiruma, hello.
- Good to see you again.

187
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:50,836
Yes sir.

188
00:12:52,004 --> 00:12:54,907
As for the rest of you, it's been a while.

189
00:12:54,974 --> 00:12:55,875
Kitano?

190
00:12:56,542 --> 00:12:57,443
Why is he here?

191
00:12:57,510 --> 00:13:00,479
Well, I don't think
any introduction is needed, though

192
00:13:01,013 --> 00:13:02,815
but please take note.

193
00:13:04,416 --> 00:13:06,418
Doctor Kitano is from Toutei University...

194
00:13:07,419 --> 00:13:10,656
and is currently working abroad as a
world-class surgeon.

195
00:13:11,056 --> 00:13:13,959
He receives job offers
from hospitals throughout Japan,

196
00:13:14,026 --> 00:13:15,795
but he never has accepted any.

197
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:21,200
Amazing! Director Hiruma, Bravo!

198
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:23,269
However,

199
00:13:24,003 --> 00:13:28,774
today...will mark my parting.

200
00:13:28,841 --> 00:13:31,110
What did you say?
I wasn't told about that.

201
00:13:31,177 --> 00:13:34,613
- Didn't I mention it?
- I made a contract with you.

202
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:41,287
- So now I would like to reconsider.
- No, that's...not exactly possible.

203
00:13:42,188 --> 00:13:43,455
You can't.

204
00:13:51,363 --> 00:13:52,198
Alright.

205
00:13:53,098 --> 00:13:54,400
In that case,

206
00:13:55,034 --> 00:13:58,337
we'll have the directors
resign as they wish,

207
00:13:58,804 --> 00:14:01,106
except for Deputy Director Hiruma.

208
00:14:01,574 --> 00:14:03,209
- Hiruma!
- Yes?

209
00:14:03,275 --> 00:14:06,111
You traitor!

210
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:07,947
I didn't mean anything bad from it.

211
00:14:09,281 --> 00:14:12,184
- Former Director!
- Please calm down!

212
00:14:12,251 --> 00:14:15,020
- Please take a breath.
- Stop making fun of me!

213
00:14:15,087 --> 00:14:16,555
Please calm down.

214
00:14:16,622 --> 00:14:17,756
This is ridiculous.

215
00:14:21,427 --> 00:14:23,963
Former Director, please take your leave.

216
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:26,065
Let go of me.

217
00:14:40,679 --> 00:14:42,214
For those left,

218
00:14:43,182 --> 00:14:46,252
I deeply appreciate
your compassionate decision.

219
00:14:46,952 --> 00:14:48,520
Toutei University Hospital.

220
00:14:48,587 --> 00:14:50,522
- Hooray!
- Hooray!

221
00:14:50,589 --> 00:14:52,191
- Hooray!
- Hooray!

222
00:14:52,258 --> 00:14:53,993
- Hooray!
- Hooray!

223
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:55,861
- Hooray!
- Hooray!

224
00:14:56,228 --> 00:15:00,633
<i>In 2016, medical establishments collapsed</i>
<i>and became more corrupt.</i>

225
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:05,738
<i>Medicine, which handles lives,</i>
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

226
00:15:19,118 --> 00:15:20,252
Good morning.

227
00:15:21,887 --> 00:15:22,888
Good morning.

228
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:27,459
<i>The Succeeding Director, Hiruma</i>

229
00:15:27,526 --> 00:15:29,595
<i>will now begin to make his rounds.</i>

230
00:15:34,033 --> 00:15:35,734
<i>Famous hospitals</i>

231
00:15:36,302 --> 00:15:38,537
<i>use their brand power</i>
<i>to push into the world.</i>

232
00:15:39,071 --> 00:15:41,974
<i>On the other hand, highly skilled surgeons</i>

233
00:15:42,041 --> 00:15:45,678
<i>in pursuit of a higher salary</i>
<i>were relocating to foreign countries.</i>

234
00:15:45,744 --> 00:15:49,148
<i>Healthcare entered an era</i>

235
00:15:49,214 --> 00:15:52,851
<i>of the strong preying on the weak.</i>

236
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:54,820
<i>In the midst of it,</i>

237
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:58,457
<i>Then came freelance doctors</i>
<i>who don't belong to hospitals.</i>

238
00:15:58,524 --> 00:16:01,894
<i>In other words, maverick doctors.</i>

239
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:08,267
TOUTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

240
00:16:15,007 --> 00:16:18,277
- Stop pushing!
- Stop pushing!

241
00:16:23,215 --> 00:16:24,416
You're the one pushing me!

242
00:16:30,789 --> 00:16:32,691
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

243
00:16:33,392 --> 00:16:34,493
<i>She hates groups,</i>

244
00:16:35,027 --> 00:16:36,161
<i>authority, and…</i>

245
00:16:36,762 --> 00:16:37,997
<i>being controlled.</i>

246
00:16:38,731 --> 00:16:41,934
<i>Her medical license and experience are her</i>

247
00:16:42,434 --> 00:16:43,736
<i>only weapons.</i>

248
00:16:44,703 --> 00:16:48,073
Why do we have to do this every day?

249
00:16:48,707 --> 00:16:50,976
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

250
00:16:51,477 --> 00:16:52,344
<i>Also known as</i>

251
00:16:53,045 --> 00:16:54,513
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

252
00:17:11,897 --> 00:17:14,900
I announce, as I resume

253
00:17:15,334 --> 00:17:19,071
this position as Director of
Toutei University Hospital...

254
00:17:20,139 --> 00:17:22,875
we will once again work together.

255
00:17:24,610 --> 00:17:30,949
I will do everything in my power,
to return Toutei...to its prosperity.

256
00:17:31,016 --> 00:17:32,584
We shall wipe out

257
00:17:32,651 --> 00:17:35,587
factional politics, and become
as one under my leadership.

258
00:17:35,654 --> 00:17:37,689
Let's lift up Toutei...

259
00:17:38,257 --> 00:17:43,996
and make it once again...
a household name.

260
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:45,764
Yes sir!

261
00:17:46,698 --> 00:17:49,601
Thank you for such a moving speech.

262
00:17:50,169 --> 00:17:51,270
Yes sir.

263
00:17:53,472 --> 00:17:57,342
Dr. Kitagawa from Kanazawa Hospital.
He is Chief Physician.

264
00:17:57,409 --> 00:17:58,911
Obviously a henchman.

265
00:17:58,977 --> 00:18:00,946
God, I am so moved!

266
00:18:02,381 --> 00:18:03,215
Thank you.

267
00:18:05,651 --> 00:18:07,719
Chief Surgeon, Saionji.

268
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:11,256
Any opinion from you?

269
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:20,466
Yes, sir.

270
00:18:20,899 --> 00:18:23,669
As you can see,
our chief is rather theatrical.

271
00:18:24,503 --> 00:18:26,305
He is a henchman too.

272
00:18:29,842 --> 00:18:31,443
As for Manager of Public Relation,

273
00:18:32,344 --> 00:18:35,347
we have a branding professional

274
00:18:35,914 --> 00:18:38,183
to be joining our hospital.

275
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:40,252
Please welcome, Ikuko Minami.

276
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,955
What a marvellous selection!

277
00:18:43,021 --> 00:18:46,658
They say that any hospitals
Ikuko Minami is dispatched to,

278
00:18:46,725 --> 00:18:52,764
- are sure to be top ranked.
- I look forward to working with you.

279
00:18:54,366 --> 00:18:56,768
She is the mysterious woman,
who has connections

280
00:18:56,835 --> 00:18:58,570
with big shots in politics and media.

281
00:18:58,637 --> 00:19:03,809
Any doctors who's been crossed off by her
is sure to disappear within a month.

282
00:19:03,876 --> 00:19:05,210
Director,

283
00:19:05,277 --> 00:19:08,247
- I haven't seen Deputy Director yet.
- What?

284
00:19:09,348 --> 00:19:12,784
Showing up late on the first day?

285
00:19:12,851 --> 00:19:15,554
I wonder if she's up to this job.

286
00:19:24,263 --> 00:19:25,497
Michiko Daimon.

287
00:19:27,132 --> 00:19:29,168
- Demon.
- That doctor?

288
00:19:30,335 --> 00:19:32,571
- Who is she?
- Good looking...

289
00:19:38,243 --> 00:19:41,346
Is she Succeeding Deputy Director?

290
00:19:43,315 --> 00:19:44,950
No…

291
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,319
Of course not.

292
00:19:48,287 --> 00:19:50,055
Wow, you scared me.

293
00:19:50,122 --> 00:19:51,890
Dr. Hiruma.

294
00:19:51,957 --> 00:19:54,126
Congratulations on your position.

295
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,627
Thank you.

296
00:19:58,163 --> 00:20:00,566
Speaking of which, Doctor Daimon...

297
00:20:01,667 --> 00:20:05,671
Thank you for coming in such
extreme fashion as usual.

298
00:20:07,005 --> 00:20:10,175
So what on earth brings you here?

299
00:20:10,242 --> 00:20:12,611
- Because I was told to come, of course.
- Huh?

300
00:20:12,678 --> 00:20:14,680
I didn't want to come here though.

301
00:20:25,457 --> 00:20:26,558
You!

302
00:20:28,493 --> 00:20:30,896
You call this cleaning?

303
00:20:31,797 --> 00:20:35,334
Look at all the dust that's still left.

304
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:44,042
Hey!

305
00:20:44,543 --> 00:20:45,944
Why are you here?

306
00:20:47,379 --> 00:20:50,182
Thanks for the treat in New York.

307
00:20:50,249 --> 00:20:51,950
You're dressed so nicely. What's up?

308
00:21:04,896 --> 00:21:06,465
Hiruma, it's been a while.

309
00:21:06,531 --> 00:21:08,700
Long time no see, Toko Kubo.

310
00:21:10,235 --> 00:21:12,604
Your evil looking has gotten worse.

311
00:21:13,238 --> 00:21:15,040
So as you.

312
00:21:16,575 --> 00:21:18,677
Hurry up and introduce the office.

313
00:21:18,744 --> 00:21:20,812
What are you talking about?

314
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:25,517
I am Deputy Director, Toko Kubo.

315
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:29,521
Kubo?

316
00:21:29,588 --> 00:21:30,722
So that means...

317
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:33,025
Shigeru Kubo is my older brother.

318
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:37,796
I am here as Deputy Director
under orders from him.

319
00:21:43,669 --> 00:21:44,903
That's who

320
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:48,040
- I hired, Michiko Daimon.
- That?

321
00:21:48,106 --> 00:21:51,076
You will pay me back for New York.

322
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:53,478
Akira, what is this?

323
00:21:54,379 --> 00:21:55,647
Just as you heard.

324
00:21:55,714 --> 00:21:58,550
- Hey, bring chair for the Deputy Director.
- Yes sir.

325
00:21:59,084 --> 00:22:00,352
A little farther.

326
00:22:01,953 --> 00:22:04,089
Please, have a seat.

327
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:09,027
You're not going to sit down?

328
00:22:10,829 --> 00:22:13,799
Kubo, let me make things clear for you.

329
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:17,369
All authority of this hospital,

330
00:22:18,036 --> 00:22:22,708
as well as responsibility,
lies in my hands.

331
00:22:23,275 --> 00:22:25,510
You are no more than a Deputy Director,

332
00:22:25,577 --> 00:22:28,380
I will not allow you to do
anything out of my control.

333
00:22:28,947 --> 00:22:31,850
- Am I right, gentlemen?
- Yes sir!

334
00:22:31,917 --> 00:22:32,851
Shut up!

335
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:38,290
My brother had to leave this hospital,

336
00:22:38,724 --> 00:22:40,392
before achieving his goal

337
00:22:41,393 --> 00:22:43,462
to reconstruct this organization.

338
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:47,332
For his sake, I will not let you ruin it.

339
00:22:49,434 --> 00:22:51,737
Stop trying to act so tough like that.

340
00:22:56,775 --> 00:23:00,312
All this is just causing another drama.

341
00:23:04,483 --> 00:23:06,017
So she isn't a cleaning lady.

342
00:23:07,486 --> 00:23:08,320
Yes sir.

343
00:23:08,387 --> 00:23:10,922
Before we formalize the contract,

344
00:23:10,989 --> 00:23:15,160
allow me to confirm
her terms of employment.

345
00:23:15,961 --> 00:23:18,063
Help professors with
their research papers.

346
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:19,030
I decline.

347
00:23:19,097 --> 00:23:21,833
- Driving professors to golf course.
- I decline.

348
00:23:21,900 --> 00:23:26,905
- Attending drinking parties.
- I don't care about it!

349
00:23:26,972 --> 00:23:29,574
All I want is to save the patients

350
00:23:29,641 --> 00:23:32,544
from this rotten organization.

351
00:23:32,611 --> 00:23:36,915
That's why I need Michiko Daimon's help!

352
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:45,056
Then why did you lie about
being a cleaning lady?

353
00:23:45,123 --> 00:23:49,094
I want this hospital to
literally get a total cleaning.

354
00:23:52,964 --> 00:23:54,366
Doctor Daimon,

355
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:58,136
that's why I need you.

356
00:23:58,870 --> 00:24:01,106
Please, help me!

357
00:24:02,374 --> 00:24:05,510
There's something shady about her.

358
00:24:06,044 --> 00:24:10,482
Sure, that old woman may seem suspicious,
but aren't you used to those things?

359
00:24:10,549 --> 00:24:12,250
Yeah, but...

360
00:24:12,317 --> 00:24:14,986
Hey, why is this person here?

361
00:24:15,053 --> 00:24:16,855
- I wanted to ask the same thing.
- Yes!

362
00:24:18,523 --> 00:24:21,526
Doctor Kaji is lonely
since he lost his former buddies.

363
00:24:21,593 --> 00:24:24,529
Yeah. I was the only one
that got to return to Toutei.

364
00:24:24,930 --> 00:24:26,465
Dr. Hara is still in Kanazawa,

365
00:24:26,865 --> 00:24:29,100
Chief Surgeon Ebina
has been sent off somewhere.

366
00:24:29,167 --> 00:24:31,470
Did he do something?

367
00:24:31,536 --> 00:24:34,539
It's because he didn't do anything
that he was sent off.

368
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:37,075
- That's right.
- Hurry up and go.

369
00:24:38,076 --> 00:24:40,145
I wonder how they're doing.

370
00:24:44,716 --> 00:24:46,218
Hurry up!

371
00:24:46,284 --> 00:24:49,387
Every doctor that came across you
has been running out of luck!

372
00:24:51,823 --> 00:24:53,859
I'm sorry Doctor Kaji,

373
00:24:53,925 --> 00:24:55,994
I win!

374
00:25:00,632 --> 00:25:04,002
- It's your fault I'm out of luck.
- How about you go home?

375
00:25:04,436 --> 00:25:05,270
No.

376
00:25:06,905 --> 00:25:08,273
Akira,

377
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:11,343
what is up with that
shady Deputy Director?

378
00:25:11,409 --> 00:25:14,412
Toko Kubo,
graduated from Toutei University,

379
00:25:14,479 --> 00:25:16,448
taking advantage of
her strong ambition and

380
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:19,951
the position as
former Director Kubo's sister,

381
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:21,486
she is the first female

382
00:25:21,553 --> 00:25:24,689
to gain position
as Chief gynaecologist in Toutei History.

383
00:25:24,756 --> 00:25:27,459
I will take revenge for you, brother.
Trust me.

384
00:25:27,959 --> 00:25:29,060
Ten years ago,

385
00:25:29,494 --> 00:25:32,464
she lost in a promotion battle
with Professor Hiruma,

386
00:25:32,931 --> 00:25:36,101
and desperately flew to the United States.

387
00:25:41,673 --> 00:25:43,275
"Michiko Daimon."

388
00:25:44,876 --> 00:25:46,778
Skills, surgery.

389
00:25:46,845 --> 00:25:48,313
Hobbies, surgery?

390
00:25:54,085 --> 00:25:56,788
Oh, no, this was so expensive!

391
00:25:57,556 --> 00:25:59,391
The clothes were so expensive!

392
00:25:59,457 --> 00:26:01,960
Skills, personal investigation.

393
00:26:02,027 --> 00:26:03,995
Hobbies, personal investigation.

394
00:26:04,062 --> 00:26:08,066
So she may have been keeping marks
on you from New York.

395
00:26:08,133 --> 00:26:10,502
- What?
- It's on me!

396
00:26:11,436 --> 00:26:15,240
Be careful. There's no such thing
as a free dinner, you know.

397
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,444
I win!

398
00:26:19,511 --> 00:26:23,148
I got all.

399
00:26:26,952 --> 00:26:29,654
We will begin this week's
pre-operation conference.

400
00:26:29,721 --> 00:26:31,856
Our first case is a 28-year-old

401
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:34,059
IT company manager, Mr. Jun Ichiki.

402
00:26:34,392 --> 00:26:35,927
His diagnose is Chordoma.

403
00:26:35,994 --> 00:26:38,597
Please welcome the doctor
in charge, Doctor Kitano.

404
00:26:42,133 --> 00:26:44,803
The tumour is located
on the base of the skull

405
00:26:44,869 --> 00:26:47,572
where spinal cord, brainstem,
arteries and nerves converge.

406
00:26:47,639 --> 00:26:49,341
This makes its removal very difficult.

407
00:26:49,407 --> 00:26:52,177
The cancer has spread
to the first cervical vertebrae,

408
00:26:52,243 --> 00:26:55,380
which means a cervical spine transplant
will be needed.

409
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:58,016
Can you remove such a complicated tumour?

410
00:26:58,483 --> 00:26:59,651
Leave it to me.

411
00:26:59,718 --> 00:27:03,855
I don't mean to doubt your skills
as a world-acclaimed super doctor,

412
00:27:04,322 --> 00:27:06,391
but if you fail,
you won't get away with it.

413
00:27:07,058 --> 00:27:09,794
As you know, it's a very important case.

414
00:27:20,572 --> 00:27:21,773
Let me do it.

415
00:27:23,241 --> 00:27:25,043
Were you not listening?

416
00:27:25,110 --> 00:27:27,946
It's a very important operation
to revive the image of Toutei.

417
00:27:28,013 --> 00:27:29,748
- A part-timer like you...
- I can do it.

418
00:27:29,814 --> 00:27:30,982
I was speaking!

419
00:27:31,049 --> 00:27:33,785
I wasn't finished!
I saw your operation in New York,

420
00:27:34,619 --> 00:27:36,821
but this patient is impossible for you.

421
00:27:38,590 --> 00:27:40,291
We will use this in this operation.

422
00:27:44,796 --> 00:27:48,366
- What is the procedure?
- We have made a titanium cervical spine,

423
00:27:48,433 --> 00:27:52,337
using a 3D printer,
to replace the affected area.

424
00:27:53,338 --> 00:27:55,240
The area is where nerves converge,

425
00:27:55,306 --> 00:27:58,376
which requires precise configuration
to match the patient.

426
00:27:59,310 --> 00:28:03,715
With this perfect replication
of the patient's cervical spine,

427
00:28:03,782 --> 00:28:09,020
this transplant surgery is what I call
"The one and only bone in the world."

428
00:28:11,489 --> 00:28:13,892
If it succeeds,
it will be the first in Japan,

429
00:28:13,958 --> 00:28:16,728
and even one of the
few rare cases in the world.

430
00:28:16,795 --> 00:28:18,396
Exactly.

431
00:28:19,931 --> 00:28:24,335
Kitano, you have had quite
a successful career, haven't you.

432
00:28:26,071 --> 00:28:30,542
When I did the Prime Minister's...
heart surgery,

433
00:28:30,608 --> 00:28:31,876
When was this?

434
00:28:31,943 --> 00:28:33,244
It was in 1989.

435
00:28:34,946 --> 00:28:35,914
In a bitterly

436
00:28:37,248 --> 00:28:39,684
- cold winter...
- We'll hear your stories later.

437
00:28:39,751 --> 00:28:40,719
At that time...

438
00:28:40,785 --> 00:28:44,589
The 3D printed parts
has already been ordered from abroad.

439
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:48,193
Is there anything else
you wish to say, Chief?

440
00:28:49,427 --> 00:28:50,261
No.

441
00:28:51,129 --> 00:28:54,866
Big surgery performed by a big name.
We are looking forward to you,

442
00:28:55,433 --> 00:28:58,303
you are indeed a super doctor
chosen by Director Hiruma.

443
00:29:09,147 --> 00:29:12,217
Director, what would you like to do
with these flowers?

444
00:29:12,283 --> 00:29:13,952
From Kawagoe Chemicals?

445
00:29:14,018 --> 00:29:16,121
Place it in the bathroom.

446
00:29:16,187 --> 00:29:19,157
Okay. Stingy flowers
could be placed in a toilet.

447
00:29:24,195 --> 00:29:25,830
Director,

448
00:29:25,897 --> 00:29:27,732
I have brought President Ichiki.

449
00:29:27,799 --> 00:29:30,235
Hello, President Ichiki.

450
00:29:30,301 --> 00:29:32,070
Please come in.

451
00:29:32,137 --> 00:29:34,706
Have a seat here, please.

452
00:29:36,574 --> 00:29:39,911
I'm so pleased you came.

453
00:29:39,978 --> 00:29:42,113
How is your condition?

454
00:29:43,414 --> 00:29:45,283
May I ask what you are doing?

455
00:29:46,551 --> 00:29:48,520
I'm broadcasting you on SNS.

456
00:29:48,586 --> 00:29:49,454
Broadcasting?

457
00:29:51,156 --> 00:29:53,758
<i>I heard you are also a graduate</i>
<i>of Toutei University.</i>

458
00:29:53,825 --> 00:29:54,659
What about it?

459
00:29:54,726 --> 00:29:56,394
<i>As fellow graduates,</i>

460
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:59,564
we can bring our hands together
to overcome your disease.

461
00:29:59,631 --> 00:30:02,167
Your surgeon, Doctor Kitano

462
00:30:02,233 --> 00:30:04,669
<i>is known as a super doctor.</i>

463
00:30:05,036 --> 00:30:07,772
<i>Please put your mind at ease.</i>

464
00:30:07,839 --> 00:30:11,910
<i>I can assure you his operating skills,</i>
<i>and that you are in safe hands.</i>

465
00:30:13,444 --> 00:30:14,546
Okay.

466
00:30:14,612 --> 00:30:18,016
Do you remember our university's
fight song, "One and Only"?

467
00:30:18,082 --> 00:30:20,451
We use that as our hospital song as well.

468
00:30:20,518 --> 00:30:24,489
How about, singing that song
before the surgery

469
00:30:24,556 --> 00:30:26,791
so that all of us can get cheered up.

470
00:30:26,858 --> 00:30:29,260
- Shall we sing it?
- What a splendid idea.

471
00:30:29,327 --> 00:30:31,629
Let's sing together. Rika, music please!

472
00:30:33,164 --> 00:30:36,835
It's one-of-a-kind

473
00:30:36,901 --> 00:30:40,839
We're unrivalled

474
00:30:40,905 --> 00:30:45,310
No strong wind can defeat us

475
00:30:45,376 --> 00:30:48,980
We keep marching forward

476
00:30:49,047 --> 00:30:53,618
Toutei…

477
00:30:53,685 --> 00:30:57,222
Our school is our pride

478
00:30:57,288 --> 00:31:01,059
It's one-of-a-kind.

479
00:31:01,125 --> 00:31:03,094
- Yes!
- You have a great voice.

480
00:31:03,161 --> 00:31:05,763
- Oh, not as good as you.
- Thank you boys.

481
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:09,367
Are these guys okay?

482
00:31:10,501 --> 00:31:14,873
The origin of our pride It is…

483
00:31:16,140 --> 00:31:17,408
I'm so bored.

484
00:31:26,651 --> 00:31:28,419
THIS HOSPITAL IS DOOMED…

485
00:31:28,486 --> 00:31:29,954
THESE GUYS ARE CRAZY

486
00:31:40,265 --> 00:31:43,568
Are all the doctors here
graduates from Toutei?

487
00:31:44,969 --> 00:31:47,405
I went to Cuba Cubanacan Medical School.

488
00:31:49,674 --> 00:31:50,508
No wonder.

489
00:31:52,477 --> 00:31:55,713
You seem kind of different
than most doctors here.

490
00:31:56,648 --> 00:31:59,684
- What?
- Oh, I mean it in a good way.

491
00:32:00,785 --> 00:32:04,155
Are you the IT person we are going
to operate on soon?

492
00:32:05,523 --> 00:32:09,360
In the IT industry, it doesn't matter
which school you are from.

493
00:32:09,427 --> 00:32:11,162
Intelligence matters the most.

494
00:32:13,197 --> 00:32:16,034
But, these doctors here...

495
00:32:17,035 --> 00:32:19,437
They're all like educational background
wearing doctor's robes?

496
00:32:20,738 --> 00:32:21,606
Exactly.

497
00:32:22,607 --> 00:32:25,276
I'm kind of starting to worry
about my surgery.

498
00:32:29,380 --> 00:32:32,317
Say... Why don't you let me do
your operation?

499
00:32:33,351 --> 00:32:35,086
Are you good at surgery?

500
00:32:35,153 --> 00:32:37,155
Yes, very.

501
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:41,559
Do you have experience performing
spine surgery with 3D printed parts?

502
00:32:42,393 --> 00:32:43,227
No.

503
00:32:46,431 --> 00:32:47,265
Oh, you don't?

504
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:48,633
What the heck.

505
00:32:56,774 --> 00:32:58,843
How boring.

506
00:33:00,178 --> 00:33:02,347
For the chordoma in this case,

507
00:33:02,413 --> 00:33:04,515
we will use this 3D part...

508
00:33:04,582 --> 00:33:06,784
It's been said that when Doctor Kitano...

509
00:33:06,851 --> 00:33:09,454
was a student at Toutei University,

510
00:33:09,887 --> 00:33:13,491
he was way behind his class,
ranked 190 out of 200 students.

511
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:14,692
Any questions?

512
00:33:15,093 --> 00:33:18,262
Even after he became a doctor
he was always made fun of...

513
00:33:18,329 --> 00:33:20,164
and not allowed to perform surgeries.

514
00:33:20,231 --> 00:33:23,368
That's the reason he decided
to transfer to America...

515
00:33:23,434 --> 00:33:25,937
or so it says in this book.

516
00:33:26,437 --> 00:33:28,539
There are students like that
who study abroad.

517
00:33:28,606 --> 00:33:32,176
In Japan, if you are the nail that
sticks out, you get hammered in.

518
00:33:32,243 --> 00:33:33,511
You're one of those, right?

519
00:33:34,579 --> 00:33:35,413
Yeah, well...

520
00:33:36,047 --> 00:33:38,783
- But he's gone too far in this cover.
- It is horrible.

521
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:40,184
Look at him.

522
00:33:40,251 --> 00:33:44,122
- This part's definitely edited.
- And look how white he is!

523
00:33:44,188 --> 00:33:46,391
It's just too strange looking...

524
00:33:47,992 --> 00:33:49,394
The first surgery

525
00:33:49,460 --> 00:33:54,165
using 3D printed parts in Japan,
will without doubt, be a success.

526
00:33:56,501 --> 00:34:01,272
The patient that the surgery will
be performed on, is this man.

527
00:34:01,339 --> 00:34:04,275
Please give a large round
of applause to...

528
00:34:04,342 --> 00:34:07,245
these two big names
our hospital is very proud of.

529
00:34:07,979 --> 00:34:09,213
Before that,

530
00:34:09,847 --> 00:34:12,884
as a patient
I have an announcement to make.

531
00:34:12,950 --> 00:34:15,119
- Announcement?
- What could it be?

532
00:34:15,186 --> 00:34:17,455
I will be broadcasting the surgery,

533
00:34:17,522 --> 00:34:22,026
live on our video broadcasting site.

534
00:34:32,203 --> 00:34:35,006
<i>It is a public viewing surgery</i>
<i>using internet.</i>

535
00:34:35,072 --> 00:34:37,141
<i>It's an unprecedented open surgery!</i>

536
00:34:37,208 --> 00:34:39,010
<i>Honestly,</i>

537
00:34:39,677 --> 00:34:41,946
<i>I do not trust this hospital.</i>

538
00:34:43,514 --> 00:34:47,385
<i>The big name of Japanese universities</i>
<i>doesn't mean anything in the world.</i>

539
00:34:48,252 --> 00:34:52,223
<i>And still the doctors here are</i>
<i>clinging to their pride.</i>

540
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:55,927
<i>How did you come up with this idea?</i>

541
00:34:55,993 --> 00:34:58,396
<i>I do not want them to fail.</i>

542
00:35:00,398 --> 00:35:02,667
<i>Behind closed door in the operating room,</i>

543
00:35:02,733 --> 00:35:06,804
<i>as a patient, I have no way</i>
<i>to know what happened.</i>

544
00:35:06,871 --> 00:35:09,040
To prevent the doctors
from doing as they please,

545
00:35:10,408 --> 00:35:12,410
I decided to broadcast it.

546
00:35:12,477 --> 00:35:15,546
Wait a minute, please.
There is a compliance problem.

547
00:35:17,482 --> 00:35:20,251
If they refuse my request,

548
00:35:21,252 --> 00:35:23,588
I will decline the surgery.

549
00:35:28,392 --> 00:35:29,560
Okay, okay.

550
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:32,430
As for the patients' request,

551
00:35:33,598 --> 00:35:36,067
we will... be happy to accommodate it.

552
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:38,569
Director...

553
00:35:38,636 --> 00:35:39,504
What do you think?

554
00:35:39,570 --> 00:35:42,306
If we can have you
exchange a firm handshake

555
00:35:42,740 --> 00:35:45,476
and perhaps have a picture or two taken...

556
00:35:48,179 --> 00:35:50,448
Great, shake hands.

557
00:35:50,515 --> 00:35:51,616
Idiot.

558
00:35:52,016 --> 00:35:53,384
Yes, go ahead.

559
00:35:53,718 --> 00:35:55,853
Idiot…

560
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:03,494
The medical field is advancing rapidly,

561
00:36:03,561 --> 00:36:06,430
with things like robot surgery
and cyber-knifes...

562
00:36:06,831 --> 00:36:09,467
Pretty soon surgeons will lose their jobs.

563
00:36:13,604 --> 00:36:16,908
Oh my, this is delicious! Fantastic!

564
00:36:16,974 --> 00:36:19,577
I'm getting great at cooking.

565
00:36:19,644 --> 00:36:22,079
I'm going to eat without you.

566
00:36:25,216 --> 00:36:26,284
Ah, wait!

567
00:36:29,420 --> 00:36:31,322
- This is...
- What's wrong?

568
00:36:31,722 --> 00:36:34,258
This is Ichiki's MRI pictures
from this morning.

569
00:36:36,227 --> 00:36:37,795
The tumour has spread.

570
00:36:38,896 --> 00:36:41,832
The 3D printed parts we ordered
won't be big enough.

571
00:36:42,934 --> 00:36:45,036
Just as I thought.

572
00:36:45,436 --> 00:36:47,305
We need to do the surgery right away.

573
00:36:49,173 --> 00:36:51,642
Kitano! Kitano!

574
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:53,911
Kitano!

575
00:36:59,417 --> 00:37:00,251
Deputy Director.

576
00:37:00,318 --> 00:37:01,319
Doctor Daimon,

577
00:37:02,753 --> 00:37:04,288
do you have a minute?

578
00:37:08,859 --> 00:37:12,230
You'd better not try
to get in the way of today's surgery.

579
00:37:12,964 --> 00:37:14,298
Huh? Why?

580
00:37:15,032 --> 00:37:17,235
Because you're too good.

581
00:37:17,668 --> 00:37:19,170
Don't help.

582
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:22,039
I will pay your reward for today,
so go home now.

583
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:27,111
If we don't operate today,
the patient will die.

584
00:37:28,145 --> 00:37:29,447
So?

585
00:37:31,816 --> 00:37:33,484
That has nothing to do

586
00:37:33,551 --> 00:37:35,886
with a part-timer like you.

587
00:37:38,990 --> 00:37:40,591
What is that look?

588
00:37:41,492 --> 00:37:44,095
I'm the one who employed you!

589
00:37:46,030 --> 00:37:47,231
Say "Yes ma'am."

590
00:37:48,899 --> 00:37:49,867
Say it!

591
00:37:51,369 --> 00:37:52,203
I decline.

592
00:37:54,071 --> 00:37:56,007
Michiko Daimon, wait right there!

593
00:38:04,115 --> 00:38:07,251
There is no way we can stop it now!
What are you thinking?

594
00:38:07,318 --> 00:38:09,153
Your blood-pressure is going up.

595
00:38:09,220 --> 00:38:10,888
Oh, I'm sorry.

596
00:38:10,955 --> 00:38:12,323
He's right.

597
00:38:12,723 --> 00:38:14,859
We already held the big press conference.

598
00:38:14,925 --> 00:38:19,063
But the tumour is rapidly growing
and has reached to the second layer.

599
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:22,266
The material we ordered will not
be able to cover everything.

600
00:38:22,633 --> 00:38:24,635
Please give me some time to resolve this.

601
00:38:24,702 --> 00:38:26,937
- How long?
- Two weeks.

602
00:38:27,004 --> 00:38:28,472
No, I can't wait!

603
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:34,645
After all the those interviews,
you have to do the operation.

604
00:38:36,180 --> 00:38:37,381
I don't hear "Yes sir."

605
00:38:38,449 --> 00:38:44,288
- It's impossible.
- Well then, make the impossible possible!

606
00:38:44,355 --> 00:38:47,491
That's what a super doctor is for!

607
00:38:47,558 --> 00:38:48,959
- Am I right?
- Yes sir.

608
00:38:49,026 --> 00:38:50,127
It's not possible.

609
00:38:50,194 --> 00:38:53,998
You're the only one in this hospital
who has experience with the method.

610
00:38:54,065 --> 00:38:54,999
I'm begging you.

611
00:38:56,334 --> 00:38:57,501
Kitano, please.

612
00:38:58,703 --> 00:39:00,771
It's a matter of our reputation.

613
00:39:01,238 --> 00:39:05,309
We are fully depending on your surgery!

614
00:39:06,277 --> 00:39:09,180
Please, do the operation!

615
00:39:12,450 --> 00:39:13,884
Please!

616
00:39:16,987 --> 00:39:20,291
This is why I hate working at
Japanese University hospitals.

617
00:39:20,358 --> 00:39:24,161
I didn't come here to save your honour!

618
00:39:24,228 --> 00:39:27,498
I am the world-known Kitano!
I only perform surgeries

619
00:39:27,565 --> 00:39:32,002
that I am 100% confident with,
under perfectly prepared conditions.

620
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:35,272
I refuse to do this surgery.

621
00:39:42,246 --> 00:39:43,114
Director!

622
00:39:44,415 --> 00:39:45,383
I can't breathe.

623
00:39:48,819 --> 00:39:49,820
Please do your best.

624
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:51,722
We will.

625
00:39:56,260 --> 00:39:59,597
Please take a deep breath
into the oxygen mask.

626
00:40:17,581 --> 00:40:21,085
The surgeon is too late.
What's going on with him?

627
00:40:33,464 --> 00:40:35,766
This is bad, the surgeon quit.

628
00:40:36,300 --> 00:40:37,134
What?

629
00:40:43,974 --> 00:40:46,811
The surgery will begin shortly.

630
00:40:46,877 --> 00:40:48,012
The time is coming.

631
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:51,015
Please wait a little longer.

632
00:40:52,016 --> 00:40:52,883
Director.

633
00:40:54,985 --> 00:40:56,287
About today,

634
00:40:57,521 --> 00:41:01,592
Well...About the operation and...

635
00:41:02,226 --> 00:41:05,930
Dr. Kitano as you all know...

636
00:41:05,996 --> 00:41:08,966
well...we're deeply sorry
to announce that...

637
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:14,238
The question of whether
he is coming or not

638
00:41:15,506 --> 00:41:22,112
has been going for a while.
H̆owever, we as the hospital...

639
00:41:22,179 --> 00:41:26,183
Since Director Hiruma
seems to be confused,

640
00:41:26,250 --> 00:41:29,753
I, Deputy Director Toko Kubo
shall explain this situation

641
00:41:30,721 --> 00:41:33,657
- The operation today is cancelled.
- What?

642
00:41:35,359 --> 00:41:37,595
- Isn't that a woman?!
- Who is that?

643
00:41:48,272 --> 00:41:49,106
You're so late.

644
00:41:49,540 --> 00:41:51,675
Are you serious?

645
00:41:52,943 --> 00:41:56,413
Doctor Daimon!

646
00:41:56,480 --> 00:42:02,219
- This is... My chest feels tight.
- Director! Are you okay?

647
00:42:02,686 --> 00:42:04,255
You'll be okay.

648
00:42:04,321 --> 00:42:05,956
Get me something to drink.

649
00:42:12,062 --> 00:42:13,797
We will now begin the removal

650
00:42:13,864 --> 00:42:17,501
of the cervical spine tumour
via nasal and oral endoscopy

651
00:42:17,568 --> 00:42:20,271
along with the transplant of
3D printed parts.

652
00:42:20,337 --> 00:42:21,705
Endoscope.

653
00:42:22,106 --> 00:42:22,973
Here you are.

654
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,174
- Suction.
- Here.

655
00:42:37,821 --> 00:42:39,356
Look at those eyes!

656
00:42:39,423 --> 00:42:40,691
She seems tough.

657
00:43:05,716 --> 00:43:08,385
Stop it!
What's a part-timer doing in here!

658
00:43:08,452 --> 00:43:10,654
I told you not to get into this!

659
00:43:10,721 --> 00:43:11,622
Shut up!

660
00:43:12,489 --> 00:43:15,059
Assistant, hold the endoscope
as still as possible.

661
00:43:15,459 --> 00:43:16,460
I know.

662
00:43:18,596 --> 00:43:19,597
You're in the way!

663
00:43:21,332 --> 00:43:22,466
You are too!

664
00:43:24,735 --> 00:43:27,137
- Oh no!
- What happened?

665
00:43:27,204 --> 00:43:29,206
- Did something happen?
- Did he die?

666
00:43:31,175 --> 00:43:32,676
Why did it go off?

667
00:43:32,743 --> 00:43:33,844
What are they doing?

668
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:45,089
Insertion of nasal speculum complete.
Scalpel.

669
00:43:54,698 --> 00:43:55,532
Hey,

670
00:43:56,467 --> 00:43:58,402
you're not following Dr. Kitano's method.

671
00:44:04,808 --> 00:44:07,444
That is not Kitano's method.

672
00:44:07,511 --> 00:44:08,345
What?

673
00:44:09,046 --> 00:44:09,980
Did she fail?

674
00:44:12,449 --> 00:44:14,151
That's why I told you to stop!

675
00:44:14,218 --> 00:44:17,154
Messing up the surgery
that holds the fate of Toutei University!

676
00:44:26,597 --> 00:44:30,134
By the way, have you used 3D before?

677
00:44:30,834 --> 00:44:33,771
- No, why?
- No way.

678
00:44:33,837 --> 00:44:36,073
- Suction.
- What?

679
00:44:37,174 --> 00:44:38,642
Bipolar.

680
00:44:38,709 --> 00:44:40,778
Did she just say she's never
performed a 3D surgery?

681
00:44:41,445 --> 00:44:43,213
Stop right now and evacuate the room!

682
00:44:43,614 --> 00:44:45,616
Stop! Do you want to kill him?

683
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:46,684
Shut it.

684
00:44:56,527 --> 00:44:57,895
You're going to fail!

685
00:45:01,598 --> 00:45:03,701
I never fail.

686
00:45:05,569 --> 00:45:06,904
What did she just say?

687
00:45:21,919 --> 00:45:24,588
- Removing the septum. Dissector.
- Here.

688
00:45:25,889 --> 00:45:29,460
I get it.
This way gives us wider surgical space.

689
00:45:29,526 --> 00:45:34,198
That is why this method is better suited
for Japanese with small nasal cavity.

690
00:45:36,200 --> 00:45:38,402
Is that why you changed the approach?

691
00:45:38,469 --> 00:45:40,504
She's more amazing than the super doctor!

692
00:45:40,571 --> 00:45:42,606
Stop being amazed and concentrate.

693
00:45:45,709 --> 00:45:48,345
- Expand the nasal speculum.
- Just a moment.

694
00:45:50,514 --> 00:45:53,350
Removing the anterior wall
of sphenoidal sinus. Drill.

695
00:46:13,537 --> 00:46:15,472
Confirming the tumour on the clivus.

696
00:46:15,539 --> 00:46:17,141
Excising. Ring forceps.

697
00:46:21,411 --> 00:46:27,985
ENDOSCOPY

698
00:46:39,797 --> 00:46:40,631
She's quick.

699
00:46:58,182 --> 00:47:00,317
- What's going on?
- We need the truth.

700
00:47:00,851 --> 00:47:02,653
Tell us what's going on!

701
00:47:09,426 --> 00:47:10,761
She hasn't messed up yet.

702
00:47:10,828 --> 00:47:12,062
You can do it.

703
00:47:12,596 --> 00:47:14,431
- Hang in there!
- It's going to be fine!

704
00:47:21,171 --> 00:47:23,340
- You can do it!
- We believe in you!

705
00:47:27,878 --> 00:47:29,213
Excision complete.

706
00:47:29,913 --> 00:47:31,615
Moving on to the transplant.

707
00:47:31,682 --> 00:47:33,684
What about the 3D part that's too small?

708
00:47:33,750 --> 00:47:35,118
We'll use his own bone.

709
00:47:36,019 --> 00:47:37,588
- Sterilize the grafting area.
- Yes.

710
00:47:37,654 --> 00:47:38,956
I see.

711
00:47:39,356 --> 00:47:42,292
She's going to fill in the area

712
00:47:42,359 --> 00:47:46,997
where the 3D parts couldn't cover,
with the patient's own ilium.

713
00:47:47,064 --> 00:47:47,898
I see.

714
00:47:53,637 --> 00:47:54,671
- Scalpel.
- Here.

715
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:24,768
It's complete.

716
00:48:24,835 --> 00:48:27,471
The blood pressure is 100
and the pulse is 60.

717
00:48:35,846 --> 00:48:37,648
- Good job.
- You too.

718
00:48:37,714 --> 00:48:39,516
Doctor Daimon, excellent job.

719
00:48:39,583 --> 00:48:40,517
Thank you.

720
00:48:40,584 --> 00:48:43,086
It made me nervous but...
You did a good job.

721
00:48:45,856 --> 00:48:46,924
Bravo.

722
00:49:12,883 --> 00:49:15,118
OPERATION SUCCEEDED

723
00:49:17,421 --> 00:49:19,256
YOUR COMMENT IS SENT

724
00:49:28,231 --> 00:49:30,300
- It succeeded.
- Amazing!

725
00:49:36,506 --> 00:49:38,008
Amazing!

726
00:49:49,920 --> 00:49:53,824
You're really incredible.
That was impressive.

727
00:49:53,890 --> 00:49:58,862
I'm sorry for what I said earlier today.
You know I become edgy before operations.

728
00:49:59,830 --> 00:50:02,866
Let me treat you with tasty dumplings.

729
00:50:02,933 --> 00:50:04,901
And a nice massage if you like!

730
00:50:04,968 --> 00:50:07,571
Your legs should be tired
from the long surgery.

731
00:50:07,637 --> 00:50:10,140
- Doctor Daimon.
- I decline.

732
00:50:11,575 --> 00:50:13,543
How come?

733
00:50:16,780 --> 00:50:18,315
You can't fool me again.

734
00:50:23,787 --> 00:50:25,989
I can get rid of you anytime I want.

735
00:50:28,191 --> 00:50:30,861
Gosh, you're so scary. So is your face.

736
00:50:32,029 --> 00:50:33,296
You're fired!

737
00:50:33,964 --> 00:50:35,065
Get out...

738
00:50:35,699 --> 00:50:37,434
Get out...Get the hell out!!

739
00:50:38,902 --> 00:50:41,104
It feels great!

740
00:50:42,672 --> 00:50:46,343
I'm sorry, Mr. Akira. I got fired.

741
00:50:46,410 --> 00:50:48,545
Already?

742
00:50:49,212 --> 00:50:52,082
Your surgery excited
all those audience online.

743
00:50:52,449 --> 00:50:54,351
I was expecting a big fortune.

744
00:50:54,418 --> 00:50:56,586
I said I'm sorry.

745
00:50:57,754 --> 00:51:01,458
No dinner for you tonight, Michiko.

746
00:51:05,729 --> 00:51:07,664
For the first time in Japan.

747
00:51:08,465 --> 00:51:12,769
We have succeeded the transplant surgery
using 3D printed spine

748
00:51:13,336 --> 00:51:16,306
which we call
"the one and only bone in the world."

749
00:51:20,377 --> 00:51:21,278
Please. Thank you.

750
00:51:21,344 --> 00:51:25,449
Some source tells that the surgeon was
a female doctor with very strong eyes.

751
00:51:25,515 --> 00:51:26,783
That is a false rumor.

752
00:51:27,717 --> 00:51:31,321
The surgeon performed the operation is
indeed the super doctor Kitano.

753
00:51:31,388 --> 00:51:32,656
Liars.

754
00:51:35,158 --> 00:51:38,028
- Come in.
- Excuse me.

755
00:51:41,565 --> 00:51:42,532
It's a melon for you.

756
00:51:44,468 --> 00:51:47,637
And the bill for the last operation
by surgeon Daimon Michiko

757
00:51:49,573 --> 00:51:50,707
who you fired.

758
00:51:56,113 --> 00:51:58,148
Oh, take this to the Director instead.

759
00:51:58,215 --> 00:51:59,916
Please.

760
00:51:59,983 --> 00:52:01,785
I'll just take this.

761
00:52:02,385 --> 00:52:05,188
- Now leave.
- Hold on.

762
00:52:05,255 --> 00:52:06,289
I said leave!

763
00:52:07,958 --> 00:52:09,292
Okay. I'm leaving.

764
00:52:11,995 --> 00:52:14,598
She is actually greedier than myself.

765
00:52:16,066 --> 00:52:17,400
Goodbye.

766
00:52:26,877 --> 00:52:27,711
It's too small.

767
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:33,750
The popularity of Toutei University
is skyrocketing.

768
00:52:33,817 --> 00:52:35,385
It's amazing.

769
00:52:36,386 --> 00:52:37,454
Excuse me.

770
00:52:39,456 --> 00:52:41,925
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

771
00:52:42,559 --> 00:52:43,927
This is a bill.

772
00:52:45,061 --> 00:52:47,964
You brought it over to me. Let's see. Wow!

773
00:52:48,031 --> 00:52:49,065
($100,000)

774
00:52:49,766 --> 00:52:52,769
Blast off, show off, what a big rip off.

775
00:52:53,403 --> 00:52:57,007
At any rate, her success in this operation
was the first case in Japan.

776
00:52:57,073 --> 00:52:59,109
But this is too much.

777
00:52:59,176 --> 00:53:02,612
I'm sure you know,
a hush money is included.

778
00:53:03,013 --> 00:53:03,847
Sir,

779
00:53:04,314 --> 00:53:08,451
please pay my remuneration
to Doctor Daimon.

780
00:53:09,119 --> 00:53:10,320
Pay your remuneration?

781
00:53:11,555 --> 00:53:14,491
Are you really okay with it?

782
00:53:15,759 --> 00:53:19,262
I'm not working here to make money.

783
00:53:20,163 --> 00:53:23,300
Actually, a big name like you

784
00:53:23,366 --> 00:53:26,536
may have earned bigger money in the U.S.

785
00:53:28,238 --> 00:53:29,072
Right.

786
00:53:29,139 --> 00:53:30,540
Doctor Kitano,

787
00:53:32,008 --> 00:53:35,445
Then what's your purpose...
of working here?

788
00:53:44,087 --> 00:53:48,258
Well then. We are looking forward to
working with you again.

789
00:53:48,325 --> 00:53:49,426
Wait a minute.

790
00:53:50,193 --> 00:53:53,630
Well...The bill you brought
is submitted properly.

791
00:53:54,064 --> 00:53:58,301
But what happened to my lovely melon?

792
00:53:59,402 --> 00:54:00,637
Oh, I'm sorry.

793
00:54:00,704 --> 00:54:03,640
That greedy Deputy Director took it away.

794
00:54:03,707 --> 00:54:04,708
If you will excuse me.

795
00:54:06,276 --> 00:54:07,744
She did what?

796
00:54:10,213 --> 00:54:12,415
She isn't the melon type...

797
00:54:12,482 --> 00:54:13,883
She's more like a felon.

798
00:54:13,950 --> 00:54:16,620
Michiko! You're not fired.

799
00:54:16,686 --> 00:54:20,023
What? Will you make me dinner, then?

800
00:54:20,090 --> 00:54:22,325
Are you serious? Beef stroganoff?

801
00:54:22,392 --> 00:54:23,994
All righty!

802
00:54:24,060 --> 00:54:25,962
Got it!

803
00:54:27,631 --> 00:54:29,699
Hey, kitty. Did you hear that too?

804
00:54:29,766 --> 00:54:34,004
He'll make me beef stroganoff tonight!

805
00:54:42,112 --> 00:54:44,881
I know you performed
my operation. Am I not right?

806
00:54:49,319 --> 00:54:50,153
No.

807
00:54:50,820 --> 00:54:52,889
It is just a rumour on the internet.

808
00:54:53,356 --> 00:54:56,226
Those rumours often turn out to be true,

809
00:54:56,293 --> 00:54:57,193
you know.

810
00:54:58,795 --> 00:54:59,763
Well, whatever...

811
00:55:06,336 --> 00:55:07,737
I'm actually glad it was you.

812
00:55:09,739 --> 00:55:12,676
The surgery wound is clean
and I'm feeling good.

813
00:55:13,977 --> 00:55:15,211
And I'm recovering fast.

814
00:55:17,480 --> 00:55:18,315
Good for you.

815
00:55:23,720 --> 00:55:24,888
Thank you.

816
00:55:26,423 --> 00:55:28,491
Dr. Daimon with strong eyes.

817
00:55:43,273 --> 00:55:48,378
<i>Director Hiruma will</i>
<i>now commence his rounds.</i>

818
00:56:08,198 --> 00:56:09,032
Well…

819
00:56:10,033 --> 00:56:12,702
Did you come back to see me?

820
00:56:13,870 --> 00:56:17,006
She's officially hired by Director Hiruma.

821
00:56:17,073 --> 00:56:20,009
Hold on. She's not officially hired.
She's a part-timer, right?

822
00:56:20,076 --> 00:56:21,778
- Part timers go to the end of...
- I decline.

823
00:56:21,845 --> 00:56:22,912
I'm not done talking!

824
00:56:22,979 --> 00:56:25,482
- Come on, let him finish.
- Mr. Akira, I guess it's time.

825
00:56:26,049 --> 00:56:28,017
We've been waiting for this!

826
00:56:32,422 --> 00:56:33,857
Excuse me.

827
00:56:34,724 --> 00:56:35,558
Here you go.

828
00:56:37,360 --> 00:56:38,194
Here.

829
00:56:40,997 --> 00:56:46,302
Now, allow me to clarify
Dr. Daimon's terms of employment.

830
00:56:46,369 --> 00:56:48,171
"Helping professors with research papers."

831
00:56:48,238 --> 00:56:49,139
I decline.

832
00:56:49,205 --> 00:56:50,540
I already know this.

833
00:56:50,607 --> 00:56:53,042
- "Driving doctors to golf."
- I decline.

834
00:56:53,410 --> 00:56:56,146
- "Attending drinking parties."
- I decline.

835
00:56:56,212 --> 00:56:59,015
- "Covering up people's love affairs."
- I decline.

836
00:56:59,082 --> 00:57:00,984
"Joining Director's rounds,
Professor rounds."

837
00:57:01,050 --> 00:57:01,951
I decline.

838
00:57:02,018 --> 00:57:03,119
And the list goes on.

839
00:57:03,186 --> 00:57:05,789
Any work which does not
require medical license.

840
00:57:05,855 --> 00:57:07,223
I will never do it.

841
00:57:10,126 --> 00:57:11,327
What did you just say?

842
00:57:11,394 --> 00:57:14,130
Are you going to do this every time?
The "I decline" series?

843
00:57:14,197 --> 00:57:15,031
That's all.

844
00:57:18,835 --> 00:57:21,070
Make way. She's coming through.

845
00:57:27,377 --> 00:57:29,712
MICHIKO DAIMON

846
00:57:31,881 --> 00:57:34,184
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

847
00:57:34,250 --> 00:57:38,755
<i>She hates groups, authority</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

848
00:57:39,756 --> 00:57:44,494
<i>Her medical license and experience</i>
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

849
00:57:45,528 --> 00:57:47,730
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

850
00:57:48,331 --> 00:57:49,265
<i>Also known as</i>

851
00:57:49,899 --> 00:57:51,100
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

852
00:59:09,412 --> 00:59:12,448
The poorest village chief in Japan?

853
00:59:12,515 --> 00:59:13,917
I'll pay any amount!

854
00:59:13,983 --> 00:59:18,021
- His scandal has been exposed.
- Dr. Daimon has started the surgery.

855
00:59:18,087 --> 00:59:19,923
She abandoned the surgery.

856
00:59:19,989 --> 00:59:21,624
Have you failed again?

857
00:59:21,691 --> 00:59:23,459
I haven't failed.
